  "title": "Just a stone",
  "intent": "She opens a big present from me, finds only a plain stone inside, and is let down.",
  "story": {
    "request": "a stone given as a gift",
    "setup": {
      "says": "A woman has a big red present with a yellow bow on a table.",
      "see": [
        "a table in front of her",
        "a big red box with a lid and a yellow bow",
        "she looks at you, hopeful, then at the box"
      ]
    },
    "event": {
      "says": "She lifts the lid and finds only a plain grey stone inside.",
      "see": [
        "she lifts the lid open",
        "she takes a grey stone out of the box",
        "she looks into the box again: it is empty",
        "she looks at the stone"
      ]
    },
    "reaction": {
      "says": "She is let down: she looks at you, sad, with the stone in her open hand.",
      "see": [
        "she looks at you",
        "a sad face",
        "she holds the stone out in her open hand and shakes her head",
        "her eyes go down to the stone"
      ]
    },
    "changes": [
      "Option B, the owner's idea: the present is a let-down, not a treasure.",
      "Disappointment, not a laugh: the owner judged the slip's laughter badly, and a sad face and shrug read with the faces and gestures we have.",
      "The box is about 0.44 m wide and 0.29 m high with the lid, so it reads at card size.",
      "Premise review: a lighter stone held clear of her dark top, an 'empty' look into the box, and the lid put clear of the box on a wider table.",
      "lB: she holds the lid by its edge (grip [0, 0.13, -0.2]), so her forearm stays off the lid top; she holds the stone lower (1.35 m) and further out, so her left fingers stay clear of her head.",
      "lB3: the bow is smaller and sits on her left side of the lid, off the line of her forearm as she lifts the lid by its back edge.",
      "lB5: she keeps the lid up in her right hand and does not let it fall, because a dropped lid lands against the front of the box, in the path of her left arm, in a different place each build.",
      "lB7: she holds the lid by its near edge (grip [0, 0.13, 0.2]), so the lid reaches away from her and not back along her right forearm.",
      "s8 round 3, sA: the stone is twice the size (0.24 m) so it reads on the card; she holds it palm-up below her face; no shrug; the lid is put down on a wider table; her eyes do more of each look down, so her face stays larger on the card.",
      "sB: the lid opens on a hinge on its right edge (a change, as the oven door), when her left hand lifts it; she does not carry it, so nothing swings to her legs; the put that dropped it on the floor (sA) is gone.",
      "sC: the stone grip is lower and nearer her, with a 7 cm fist, so her open palm stays under the stone; the lid reach point is 3 cm higher, above the lid top.",
      "sD: her left hand is open and flat under the stone (a 9 cm fist), so her fingers stay out of it; the lid reach stops 3 cm short of the lid top."
    ]
  },
